              "file": "src/BuildingBlocks/Web/Realtime/HeroRealtimeExtensions.cs",
              "line": 56,
              "description": "The `userIds` query parameter is fully client-controlled and is used directly as the lookup key set into the global, non-tenant-scoped `IPresenceTracker` singleton. The only gate is `.RequireAuthorization()` (any authenticated user of the platform) — there is no check that the caller shares a tenant, channel, or any other relationship with the target user ids before returning their online/offline status. Also CWE-862: GET /api/v1/realtime/presence takes an attacker-controlled, comma-separated list of arbitrary userIds from the query string and returns each one's online/offline status straight from the process-wide IPresenceTracker singleton. The only guard is `.RequireAuthorization()` (any authenticated user of any tenant) — there is no check that the caller shares a tenant, channel, or any other relationship with the requested userIds.",
              "exploit_scenario": "A low-privileged user in Tenant A authenticates, obtains a JWT, then calls GET /api/v1/realtime/presence?userIds=<guid-from-tenant-B>,<guid-from-tenant-B-2> and receives each target's live online/offline status, even though they have no membership or relationship with Tenant B or its users.",
